    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d39-a4">

                <pb facs="0138" n="54" sameAs="frus:frus1886/pg54"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 4 in No. 325.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Baiz to Mr.
                            Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Consulate-General of Honduras in the United States of
                                America</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">New York</hi></placeName>,
                            <date calendar="gregorian" when="1886-01-18"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >January</hi> 18, 1886</date>. (Received January
                    19.)</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor of owning the receipt of
                    the communications of your excellency, dated 7th and 12th instant, and in reply
                    beg to tender best thanks, in the name of my Government, for the efficient
                    measures adopted towards preventing a violation of the neutrality laws on the
                    part of any individuals against the Republic of Honduras, which I have the honor
                    of representing.</p>
                <p>I shall consider it my duty to inform your excellency of any new occurrences that
                    may transpire, regarding the revolutionary movements in question, and remain,
                    &amp;c.</p>
                <closer><signed>JACOB BAIZ,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Consul-General.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
